#* {{quote-text|en|year=1937|author={{w|Zora Neale Hurston}}|title={{w|Their Eyes Were Watching God}}|url=https://archive.org/details/theireyeswerewat00hur_a4l|chapter=5|page=66|publisher=University of Illinois Press|year_published=1978
|passage=Janie was astonished to see the money Jody had spent for the land come back to him so fast. Ten new families bought lots and moved to town in six weeks. It all looked too big and '''rushing''' for her to keep track of.}}